  "description": "A free, MIT-licensed mediator for .NET, shaped like MediatR 11 — a drop-in alternative for teams moving off MediatR now that it requires a paid licence. Requests and responses, commands returning nothing, notifications (Publish/INotification), streamed sequences (IStreamRequest), and pipeline behaviors around all of them, via IMediator, ISender and IPublisher. Migration is usually a using-directive change plus AddMediatR -> AddCerise; handlers and behaviors are untouched. Also supports pre/post processors, exception handlers and exception actions in the Cerise.Pipeline namespace, and synchronous handler base classes. One dependency, .NET 8/9/10.",
